==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[rock-paper-scissors]]

===Etymology===
A calque of the handshapes in Japanese [[janken]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{label|en|games}} A popular children's [[game]] using three [[hand]] [[sign]]s representing rock, paper and scissors, frequently used as a [[tiebreaker]].

====Synonyms====
* [[paper scissors stone]]
* [[scissors paper rock]]
* [[scissors paper stone]]
* [[janken]]
* [[roshambo]], [[rochambeau]], [[row-sham-bow]], [[roe-sham-boe]]

